MID_SC14_00_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m01_001: These guards of mine are the best of the best. One of\n'em killed a bear with his bare hands!
MID_SC14_00_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m02_001: Defeated? So easily?! You lied about killing that bear,\ndidn't you? You lot couldn't kill a rabbit!
MID_SC14_00_m02_002: Even claimed you were the most skilled bodyguards\nmoney could buy. 
MID_SC14_00_m02_003: Skilled? This crew? Maybe you just shortchanged\nthem on payday.
MID_SC14_00_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m03_001: Now, now, don't let this defeat embarrass you. I am\njust very, VERY good at what I do.
MID_SC14_00_m03_002: Impressive. I'd wager this isn't just some traveler\nwe have with us.
MID_SC14_00_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m04_001: This soldier's not half bad! Those enormous arms of\nhis could split trees in half, not to mention enemies.
MID_SC14_00_m04_002: I'll have to see how this plays out, but I'd wager\nwe've got a warrior of some notoriety here.
MID_SC14_00_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m05_001: These people are all...i-incredible. I have to keep up!
MID_SC14_00_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m06_001: Well, well, I've seen my fair share of spellsongs over\nthe years, but never anything like this.
MID_SC14_00_m06_002: Yes, I think it's safe to say this is no ordinary woman.
MID_SC14_00_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m07_001: I thought I'd left that nasty bit of history dead and\nburied in a ditch long ago.
MID_SC14_00_m07_002: But here it is, alive and well, baring its fangs!
MID_SC14_00_m07_003: Ah, that little girl...just look at her. Grew into quite\nthe beeeauty. Such a shame to waste her.
MID_SC14_00_m08: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m08_001: If I don't kill this lot, I'll never escape what I did.\nThose awful flames, I just want to forget them!
MID_SC14_00_m08_002: Heh... Hehe! What does it matter. I'll never sleep\nagain without fearing for my life.
MID_SC14_00_m09: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m09_001: Here's a juicy tidbit to cling to while you die—I killed\nthe praetor who went missing en route to Cydonia!
MID_SC14_00_m09_002: Oh? I heard there was an incident with a praetor\nused to justify Arago's invasion of Cydonia.
MID_SC14_00_m09_003: Some say it was the catalyst that led Arago to seize\nthe territory. And you were involved, were you?
MID_SC14_00_m10: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_m10_001: I'm gonna hurt you till every bone in your body\nwishes you never went against Bjor the Magnificent!
MID_SC14_00_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_e01_001: If you get injured, I'll gladly provide some healing.
MID_SC14_00_e03: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_e03_001: I'm going to sing a lullaby that sends you lot to hell!
MID_SC14_00_e04: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_e04_001: Not the pushovers I thought they'd be. Bodyguards!
MID_SC14_00_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_00_e05_001: We've done what we came here to do—but his\ncronies still have some fight in them.
MID_SC14_01_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_m01_001: Haha! Stupid moths, flying straight into the flame.
MID_SC14_01_m01_002: Come at me! Feel the fire!
MID_SC14_01_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_m02_001: Milady, look there—enemies with bows.
MID_SC14_01_m02_002: Be careful, they'll fire on us if we get too close.
MID_SC14_01_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_m03_001: Some accounts claim that Drake's treasures have the\npower to take control of the world.
MID_SC14_01_m03_002: To possess something like this would mean existing\non an entirely other level from lords or the like.
MID_SC14_01_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_m04_001: I want my mother back, Balboa!
MID_SC14_01_m04_002: Shut up, you obnoxious brat! I don't want to hear\nanother word about that woman!
MID_SC14_01_m04_003: Who is this child's mother? What is it about her that\nhas this snake so rattled?
MID_SC14_01_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_m05_001: I hear you took out Bjor and his crew.
MID_SC14_01_m05_002: You might have some skill, sure, but I promise\nI won't be going down easy like those lowlifes.
MID_SC14_01_m05_003: You see, as long as I have this, there's nobody who\ncan beat me.
MID_SC14_01_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_e01_001: Look at that. The enemy dropped a key.
MID_SC14_01_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_01_e02_002: I wonder if it opens that chest—and if that chest will\ncontain something useful.
MID_BD14_02_m01: <TH>
MID_BD14_02_m01_001: Now be a good girl and hand over somethin' that's\nworth somethin'. C'mon, give me what you got!
MID_BD14_02_m01_002: Oh ho ho, that vihuela looks like it's worth something\nshiny. I'll take that.
MID_BD14_02_m01_003: Oho! I didn't think I'd be attacked here, of all places.\nVery careless of me.
MID_BD14_02_m01_004: My business here may have been minor, but still\nyou are taking up my time.
MID_BD14_02_m01_005: Have you no idea the fate you're inviting upon\nyourself? I suppose I'll need to show you.
MID_BD14_02_m02: <TH>
MID_BD14_02_m02_001: Hold it! The two of you, against a woman all on\nher own?
MID_BD14_02_m02_002: Well, this is a surprise. What an incredible beauty.
MID_BD14_02_m03: <TH>
MID_BD14_02_m03_001: There's that feeling—Obsidian is resonating. But it's\nnever happened quite like this before.
MID_BD14_02_m02_004: {SetColor=Gray}Hmm... Impressive the way she's able to make\nObsidian sing like that.{SetColor=Default}
MID_BD14_02_m02_005: {SetColor=Gray}She must be quite skilled, no doubt thanks to the\nbloodline she inherited.{SetColor=Default}
MID_BD14_02_m04: <TH>
MID_BD14_02_m04_001: The Rose of Caelus?! What are you doing here?
MID_BD14_02_m05: <TH>
MID_BD14_02_m05_001: You there! Please do not fret. I am here and, I assure\nyou, everything will be alright.
MID_SC14_03_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_m01_001: Exactly as I expected, Leilidahna. You've spent your\ntime away honing your skills, haven't you?
MID_SC14_03_m01_002: It pleases me to see you were not just lazing about\nwhile in hiding.
MID_SC14_03_m01_003: See, this is what makes us the perfect rivals—we\nchallenge and motivate each other!
MID_SC14_03_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_m02_001: You really have changed, Olympia. You're much\nmore skilled.
MID_SC14_03_m02_002: Yes, yes, I am. Very much so, Leilidahna!
MID_SC14_03_m02_003: I have gone to painstaking efforts to improve just so\nthat, one day, you will have to acknowledge me!
MID_SC14_03_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_m03_001: You have no idea how hard I've worked to make sure\nthat I could beat you when the time came.
MID_SC14_03_m03_002: Now I will show you what I've made of myself and\nlaugh—HAHA—when you gag on the taste of defeat!
MID_SC14_03_m03_003: Ha! Please, show me what you can do. Here\nI come, Olympia!
MID_SC14_03_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_m04_001: I must confess, I do find you rather intolerable.
MID_SC14_03_m04_002: Tut-tut, Syracusio. I care not one bit what you think.
MID_SC14_03_m04_003: As long as you are backing Leilidahna, then you\nare my enemy, simple as that!
MID_SC14_03_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_m05_001: I will show you that the heart of the Blue Rose of\nCaelus beats steady and strong!
MID_SC14_03_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e01_001: Listen well as I explain the rules of this contest!
MID_SC14_03_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e02_001: The team who {SetColor=Gold}captures the most brazier flames{SetColor=Default}\nwithin the {SetColor=Gold}time limit {SetColor=Default}will be declared the {SetColor=Gold}winner{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_03_e02_002: When your team captures a flame, it shall turn {SetColor=Gold}blue{SetColor=Default}.\nWhen mine does, it shall turn {SetColor=Gold}red{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_03_e03: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e03_001: There is something unique about these braziers.\nTo demonstrate! You see that blue flame there?
MID_SC14_03_e04: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e04_001: Were I to make red the braziers on either side of it,\nlike so...
MID_SC14_03_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e05_001: Voilà! The middle brazier turns red as well.\nBy {SetColor=Gold}flanking an enemy brazier{SetColor=Default}, {SetColor=Gold}you capture it{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_03_e06: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e06_001: There's another way to capture a brazier, and that is\nby using a {SetColor=Gold}spellsong{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_03_e07: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e07_001: When you do so, you'll capture all the flames {SetColor=Gold}within\nrange of the song{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_03_e07_002: Use spellsongs {SetColor=Gold}in concert with {SetColor=Default}the flanking tactic\nto seize victory!
MID_SC14_03_e08: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e08_001: Understood? Then, without further ado, let us finally\nsettle who is the superior rose!
MID_SC14_03_e11: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e11_001: Ohoho! Victory is within my grasp! Your skills\nhave dulled, my dear Leilidahna!
MID_SC14_03_e12: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e12_001: How is it I've been put on my back foot?!\nNo matter... I will defeat you, Leilidahna!
MID_SC14_03_e13: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e13_001: Time is up. Now, I shall announce the results.
MID_SC14_03_e13_002: My team's final tally of captured flames appears\nto be...{Variable=5}.
MID_SC14_03_e13_003: Meanwhile, your team's final tally was {Variable=6}.
MID_SC14_03_e14: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e14_001: Which means... *sigh* You have bested me again,\nLeilidahna.
MID_SC14_03_e15: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e15_001: Ohoho! How dreadfully sad for you—I won!
MID_SC14_03_e16: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e16_001: We will assist you, Olympia!
MID_SC14_03_e17: <TH>
MID_SC14_03_e17_001: How unsporting! This threatens the integrity of the\ncompetition.
MID_SC14_03_e17_002: I don't mind. Makes things more interesting.
MID_SC14_05_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_m01_001: Just wait, Lechner, until I slit your neck!
MID_SC14_05_m01_002: Milady, I understand your eagerness, but being\nhasty won't serve us.
MID_SC14_05_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_m02_001: Let's see now... Soldiers, kill all the men. The women,\nI'll keep!
MID_SC14_05_m02_002: Yuck... Gross. Mom warned me to stay away from\nguys like him.
MID_SC14_05_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_m03_001: I've waited a long time for this chance. Are you\nready to die, Lechner?
MID_SC14_05_m03_002: Not going to happen, girlie. Because I'm going to\nkill you first!
MID_SC14_05_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_m04_001: You've heard of me, yes? Heard the terrifying stories\nof the Mad Dog? You'll find out they're all true!
MID_SC14_05_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_m05_001: These are no ordinary soldiers. Highly skilled and\ncoordinated, using the terrain to their advantage.
MID_SC14_05_m05_002: I don't see how, even as captain of the king's guard,\nhe would have authority to command such elites.
MID_SC14_05_m05_003: I wonder if... Perhaps there's another organization\nat his back?
MID_SC14_05_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_m06_001: The stream of reinforcements is not slowing, milady.\nAnd we can only hold out for so long.
MID_SC14_05_m06_002: I suggest falling back and waiting for another chance.
MID_SC14_05_m06_003: But...damn it! I almost had him! I could practically\nfeel my hands wrapping around his neck!
MID_SC14_05_m06_004: I concur with Buccar. We'd be well advised to\nretreat, Miss Leda.
MID_SC14_05_m06_005: If it's any comfort, in his current position, Lechner\nwill be restrained from leaving Dagsion.
MID_SC14_05_m06_006: Which means we will have another opportunity.\nTrust me.
MID_SC14_05_m06_007: Fine, alright.
MID_SC14_05_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_e02_001: Damn Lechner. He's more tactical than he seems—\nand his defenses are airtight. We have to be careful.
MID_SC14_05_e02_002: Some warriors can even {SetColor=Gold}get back on their feet after\nbeing defeated{SetColor=Default}. I worry he may be one.
MID_SC14_05_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_05_e01_001: Fine, so you might be competent...but you're also\noutnumbered. Come out and play, guys!
MID_BD14_16_m01: <TH>
MID_BD14_16_m01_001: There it is. No time to waste—let's take it out.
MID_BD14_16_m01_002: What the HECK is that thing? It's not human...but it\ndoesn't look like an animal either.
MID_BD14_16_m01_003: If I were to posit a guess, I'd wager this is not its\nintended form.
MID_BD14_16_m01_004: Perhaps, say, someone attempted to summon the\nbeast, but only did so partially...
MID_BD14_16_m01_005: Eugh! That's well and good, but why does the\nPhantom look so ghastly and...unstable?
MID_BD14_16_m02: <TH>
MID_BD14_16_m02_001: Miss Leda. You wouldn't know where this Phantom\ncame from, would you?
MID_BD14_16_m02_002: No. Why the hell would I? Stop your idiotic\ntheorizing and focus on the fight!
MID_BD14_16_m03: <TH>
MID_BD14_16_m03_001: What a disturbing foe that was.
MID_BD14_16_m03_002: When did Dagsion become so dangerous?
MID_SC14_06_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m01_001: I believe we've all heard that our opponents are\nheavily armored.
MID_SC14_06_m01_002: In that case, here's what I'd suggest. We hold them\nback with obstacles and our sturdiest fighters...
MID_SC14_06_m01_003: and then blow them to bits from a distance\nwith magic. That ought to work, right?
MID_SC14_06_m01_004: We have our Salamanders as well, so I think your\nstrategy makes sense.
MID_SC14_06_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m01_005: Everyone has it right? The you-know-what?\nLet's wait for juuust the right moment to use it.
MID_SC14_06_m01_006: I'll give the signal when it's time. Hold back till then.
MID_SC14_06_m01_007: Yes, ma'am!
MID_SC14_06_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m02_001: OK... Got 'em nice and drawn in.
MID_SC14_06_m02_002: Everyone, now!
MID_SC14_06_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m02_003: Hell. They had that up their sleeves? Clever move\non their part.
MID_SC14_06_m02_004: So, they're using items to increase their resistance\nto magic. An effective tactic.
MID_SC14_06_m02_005: That will cover one of the major weaknesses of\nheavily armored soldiers.
MID_SC14_06_m02_006: What?! But if our magic won't work, then what are\nwe gonna do?!
MID_SC14_06_m02_007: Perhaps we underestimated our enemy. Any match\nin the Heroic Games is bound to be a challenge.
MID_SC14_06_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m02_008: Counterattack time. Let's rout these girls!
MID_SC14_06_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m03_001: Come on! The Heroic Games are a chance to make\nour mark.
MID_SC14_06_m03_002: Let's see to it that everyone in Dagsion knows about\nthe Rains of Palma!
MID_SC14_06_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_m04_001: Aw, just like that, huh? Well, I knew I wasn't\ngonna win anyway.
MID_SC14_06_m04_002: At least I gave them a hell of a fight... I know that'd\nmake him proud.
MID_SC14_06_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e02_001: <DLG>The armored knight used pure water.
MID_SC14_06_e03: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e03_001: I've been wondering...what is this exactly?
MID_SC14_06_e03_002: It's a guess as much as anything, but perhaps it\nproduces dry air to replicate a desert climate.
MID_SC14_06_e03_003: *gasp* Of course... Using that to dry the air might\nmean we can negate the effect of the pure water!
MID_SC14_06_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e05_001: Urgh... I can just feel my skin cracking, the air's\nso dry. But at least it's drying up that pure water!
MID_SC14_06_e06: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e06_001: Oh! What's that? A weapon? Where'd it come from?
MID_SC14_06_e15: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e15_001: Hmhm. Consider it an offering from me. Use it to\nswiftly dispatch your foes.
MID_SC14_06_e07: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e07_001: You guys just don't quit. I should've expected this.\nBut I won't be done in so easily!
MID_SC14_06_e09: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e09_001: Oh, my! What strong magic! Jasmine's defenses\nwill be so hard to break through now!
MID_SC14_06_e10: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e10_001: This must be the work of the diviner behind her.\nAnother one of her battle secrets...
MID_SC14_06_e11: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e11_001: Tough defenses. We might want to start by defeating\nthat diviner casting defensive magic.
MID_SC14_06_e13: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e13_001: I'm sorry, diviner... But your intrusive magic has\nbeen cleared from play!
MID_SC14_06_e14: <TH>
MID_SC14_06_e14_001: <DLG>Spectators have thrown items into the arena.
MID_SC14_09_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m01_001: You won't get away with this, Lechner. I will NOT\nlet you!
MID_SC14_09_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m02_001: Now, Moonstone... We shall play an ode to the\nresentment of the risen dead.
MID_SC14_09_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m03_001: Ahh, nothing like messing with your prey before you\nkill it.
MID_SC14_09_m03_004: Miss Leda, he is trying to provoke you to the\npoint of distraction. Do not let him.
MID_SC14_09_m03_005: This guy is officially the worst.
MID_SC14_09_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m04_001: Lechner, frankly, I am rather put off by your perverse\nbehavior.
MID_SC14_09_m04_002: But since now we're in the same boat, I'd prefer it\ndidn't sink.
MID_SC14_09_m04_003: Damn right. Whatever fate befalls me, it's yours too!
MID_SC14_09_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m05_001: Lechner... Allowing you into the city, all those\nyears ago, was my greatest sin.
MID_SC14_09_m05_002: And the only way to absolve myself is by killing you.
MID_SC14_09_m05_003: We'll see if you can manage. I didn't get here\nthrough connections alone. I can bite!
MID_SC14_09_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m06_001: No one who tries touching this cargo is going to\nleave here alive.
MID_SC14_09_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m07_001: Maria... Was this your intention all along? To get\nclose to me, and take advantage?
MID_SC14_09_m07_002: Oh, you know. Was it intention, was it coincidence—\nwho's to say?
MID_SC14_09_m07_003: Much more pertinent now is that I'm not going to\nabide your meddling.
MID_SC14_09_m08: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_m08_001: Will you dance for me? Hear my song, and dance\nyour way to the underworld!
MID_SC14_09_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_e01_001: Yes, that should be enough to defeat them.\nGo forward, my soldiers!
MID_SC14_09_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_e02_001: Will you be able to hear this song without crumbling?\nOhoho... I very much doubt it.
MID_SC14_09_e03: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_e03_001: Ungh... My head! I can't let that woman do this!
MID_SC14_09_e04: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_e04_001: Listen well to Moonstone's melody, imbued with all\nthe darkness of the night!
MID_SC14_09_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_e05_001: Milady, there is one more thing we set up to prepare\nfor today.
MID_SC14_09_e06: <TH>
MID_SC14_09_e06_001: Artillery? It looks like {SetColor=Gold}onagers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_09_e06_002: Yes—able to attack the enemies across the river.\nLet's put them to use.
MID_BD14_10_m01: <TH>
MID_BD14_10_m01_001: She summoned a Demonic Beast with her vihuela?\nWho is this woman?
MID_BD14_10_m01_002: You know, as startling as that monster is, I'm almost\nmore stunned by how well she plays...
MID_BD14_10_m01_003: You can't be serious, Creek. We are not here to enjoy\nthe performance!
MID_BD14_10_m02: <TH>
MID_BD14_10_m02_001: Miss Leda. I didn't know you were planning to\nsummon a Demonic Beast from the underworld...
MID_BD14_10_m02_002: That is an ominous portent. But right now, at least\nit helps us escape this predicament.
MID_BD14_10_m03: <TH>
MID_BD14_10_m03_001: Gods. I don't know what I expected today, but it was\nnot to face this bizarre-looking Demonic Beast.
MID_BD14_10_m03_002: It reminds me of the one with burning eyes we killed\nin Bau Canyon.
MID_BD14_10_m03_003: The one I saved you from, you mean? You still owe\nme for that as well.
MID_BD14_10_m03_004: Alright, alright. Let's handle this situation before we\nget stuck on that.
MID_BD14_10_m04: <TH>
MID_BD14_10_m04_001: Alright! We've taken it out. Time to accept your fate.
MID_BD14_10_m04_002: Really? I wouldn't be so sure.
MID_BD14_10_m04_003: She seems oddly...calm. You don't think she might\nhave something else up her sleeve?
MID_SC14_12_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m01_001: I hate to tell you this, but I'm starting things off\nwith everything I've got. 
MID_SC14_12_m12: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m01_002: Don't do it, Leda! The power's too dangerous!
MID_SC14_12_m01_003: Leda, you hear it too, don't you? The voice? You\ncan't obey it!
MID_SC14_12_m01_004: If you can hear the voice, then why don't you follow\nyour own advice? Go on...withdraw!
MID_SC14_12_m13: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m01_005: You're acting like an idiot! Why don't you care\nabout yourself?
MID_SC14_12_m01_006: Why can't you see that you're surrounded by people\nwho deeply care about you?
MID_SC14_12_m01_007: They all love you, Leda! And this is how you\nrepay them?
MID_SC14_12_m01_008: That's none of your business! You better shut that\nloud mouth of yours before I shut it for you!
MID_SC14_12_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m02_001: Rrr... Milady, please forgive me!
MID_SC14_12_m02_002: Buccar? What are you doing?!
MID_SC14_12_m14: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m02_003: What a mess! Have you lost your mind, Buccar?\nI'm sorry, but I won't go along with this.
MID_SC14_12_m02_004: I would give my own life if that's what it takes to\nstop you, milady.
MID_SC14_12_m02_005: I beg you to stop. This is not the way. Nothing but\nruin awaits you down this path.
MID_SC14_12_m02_006: I want only to save you from that. And if I fail, then\nI'll have failed to keep my promise to Lord Guillermo.
MID_SC14_12_m02_007: Even if you get your revenge, your heart will not\nknow peace! That much is clear to me!
MID_SC14_12_m02_008: If my life ends, it ends. But I want you to go on\nliving. I want you to find real happiness.
MID_SC14_12_m02_009: That was my promise to your father. And it's all\nI've ever wanted.
MID_SC14_12_m15: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m02_010: What? That's what this is about? That's why you're\nbetraying me?
MID_SC14_12_m02_011: This is...unforgivable! I will never, EVER, forgive you\nfor this, Buccar!
MID_SC14_12_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m03_001: I will not lose! I will save my father!
MID_SC14_12_m03_002: Curse your reasons! Stand aside, Leda!
MID_SC14_12_m03_003: Shut up! Just because you're a stupid child doesn't\nmean you're the only one with something to lose!
MID_SC14_12_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m04_001: I have my own reasons for winning at any cost.
MID_SC14_12_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m05_001: Your combat style... It's like his. It's burned into\nmemory of that day!
MID_SC14_12_m05_002: Where did you learn how to fight like that?
MID_SC14_12_m05_003: Oh, I've learned some tricks from a few places.\nPop and Bertrand, for starters.
MID_SC14_12_m05_004: Saying that man's name like it's nothing?\nHow dare you!
MID_SC14_12_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m06_001: Miss Leda, I am not an insensitive man. Understand,\nI have no desire to get in your way...
MID_SC14_12_m06_002: But I must make sure... Are you really and\ntruly alright?
MID_SC14_12_m06_003: So close... I can almost reach...his neck...
MID_SC14_12_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m07_001: Buccar! You betrayed me. I will make sure you\npay for that!
MID_SC14_12_m07_002: Do as you will. Even if I pay for it with my life, I will\nstop you, milady.
MID_SC14_12_m08: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m08_001: I never thought you would betray her. For once, I am\ntoo shocked for words.
MID_SC14_12_m08_002: Think what you will. I can only follow my heart.
MID_SC14_12_m09: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m09_001: Buccar, I just can't bring myself to believe it. You, of\nall people, betraying Leilidahna...
MID_SC14_12_m09_002: Perhaps... Perhaps there's more to it than that.\nPerhaps this is the form your loyalty takes.
MID_SC14_12_m10: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m10_001: Buccar... I don't know what to do.
MID_SC14_12_m10_002: Don't worry. You do not need to take my side in this.\nThis is my burden.
MID_SC14_12_m11: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_m11_001: I really hope Buccar's OK.
MID_SC14_12_m11_002: No one gets in my way—no one. It doesn't matter\nwho they are.
MID_SC14_12_m11_003: Do you truly mean that, Leilidahna?
MID_SC14_12_m11_004: Rrgh.
MID_SC14_12_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e01_001: What in heaven's name is that?
MID_SC14_12_e01_002: That is an {SetColor=Gold}explosive{SetColor=Default}. If you {SetColor=Gold}strike one {SetColor=Default}and {SetColor=Gold}get it\nto explode{SetColor=Default}, it may take out nearby enemies.
MID_SC14_12_e01_003: Though...our enemies will surely have a similar tactic\nin mind. Approach with caution.
MID_SC14_12_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e05_001: Ohoho... Why don't I play for you, hm? Let us dance\nin the darkness of the night and enliven this battle.
MID_SC14_12_e06: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e06_001: I hear something. Is that...Moonstone's melody?
MID_SC14_12_e08: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e08_001: The Demonic Beast isn't obeying me. And now there\nare risen dead... That damn woman!
MID_SC14_12_e09: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e09_001: Something isn't right. What the heck is going on?
MID_SC14_12_e09_002: I'm not sure myself. But we have to handle this\nDemonic Beast somehow.
MID_SC14_12_e10: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e10_001: Now, squad! Let's go!
MID_SC14_12_e11: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e11_001: I'll show them what I can do too. Let's go, squad!
MID_SC14_12_e12: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e12_001: Left flank! Advance!
MID_SC14_12_e14: <TH>
MID_SC14_12_e14_001: Ah, well... So much for our plan. Regardless, we must\nsally forth and eliminate the enemy general!
MID_SC14_13_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_m01_001: Hmph. Forgive me, but my duty is to deal with\nany threat to Her Majesty's safety.
MID_SC14_13_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_m02_001: Very impressive. There is clearly substance behind\nthe flash of your performance.
MID_SC14_13_m02_002: You've got that right. Oh, Queen Theodora, I am\njust itching to defeat you!
MID_SC14_13_m02_003: That's all I have to do, and then the White-Maned\nDemon is in striking distance!
MID_SC14_13_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_m03_001: They say a lion strikes with all her might even at a\nmere sand rabbit. I am no different.
MID_SC14_13_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_m04_001: Rarely have I met one even more stubborn\nthan me...
MID_SC14_13_m04_002: So be it. You win. I thank you for the show.
MID_SC14_13_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e01_001: Barriers! Clearly, they do not intend to allow us\nnear their leader.
MID_SC14_13_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e02_001: Our forces are divided too. We'll have to do\nsomething about that.
MID_SC14_13_e02_002: Each squad defends a barrier. Once {SetColor=Gold}we eliminate\nthem all, the barriers should fall{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC14_13_e03: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e03_001: The battlefield's divided, but it looks like I can\nwarp around with that device.
MID_SC14_13_e03_002: Each squad defends a barrier. When {SetColor=Gold}they all go down,\nso will the barriers{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC14_13_e04: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e04_001: I must prevail...and so I shall hold nothing back!
MID_SC14_13_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e05_001: This is bad. We're easy targets.
MID_SC14_13_e06: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e06_001: I recognize that device. If memory serves, it can\nmagically reinforce barriers.
MID_SC14_13_e07: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e07_001: Using that, we can {SetColor=Gold}prevent attacks from going\nbeyond the barrier{SetColor=Default}. Let's put it to use, shall we?
MID_SC14_13_e08: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e08_001: <DLG>Theodora will use Earthen Hurl in the next\nenemy phase.
MID_SC14_13_e13: <TH>
MID_SC14_13_e13_001: The barriers are gone... Tobias and the others must\nhave been defeated.
MID_SC14_13_e13_002: But I can prevail without the need for such tricks.\nCome and face me!
MID_SC14_14_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m01_001: Father... No. What happened to you?
MID_SC14_14_m01_002: It's me. It's Leilidahna! You recognize me, right?
MID_SC14_14_m01_003: Does that woman have no heart? No humanity?!\nWhat a cruel thing to do.
MID_SC14_14_m01_004: Milady... Oh, how terrible.
MID_SC14_14_m01_005: The boundless sadism of forcing a parent and child to\nkill each other! Even if one is the risen dead...
MID_SC14_14_m01_006: I'm sorry, Leda.
MID_SC14_14_m01_007: Miss Leda, you must beware. The risen dead cannot\ncomprehend the logic of the living.
MID_SC14_14_m01_008: He may look like your father, but do not think of him\nas such. His heart cannot be reached!
MID_SC14_14_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m02_001: Well then. What will you make of this?
MID_SC14_14_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m03_001: You will not escape, Rose of Caelus.
MID_SC14_14_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m04_001: Leda, keep it together! That thing's not your father.\nIt's an impostor!
MID_SC14_14_m04_002: Why, that's not true! This is your genuine father's\nsoul, as it's been captured in the underworld.
MID_SC14_14_m04_003: Ahaha. Though I'll grant that the risen dead lack the\nlove and affection they had in life.
MID_SC14_14_m04_004: All that remains is the urge to kill and raze. So you\nmay want to stop staring and fight him!
MID_SC14_14_m04_005: Aah...
MID_SC14_14_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m05_001: Father, please, I'm begging you. I don't want to\ndo this!
MID_SC14_14_m05_002: You must recognize me. It's me, Leilidahna!
MID_SC14_14_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m06_001: Who...am I? What is this place?
MID_SC14_14_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m07_001: Sometimes a bard, and at others the bewitching\nchancellor of Arago.
MID_SC14_14_m07_002: What are you planning? I want to know your\ntrue motives.
MID_SC14_14_m07_003: Really, now. Why would I tell you anything?
MID_SC14_14_m08: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m08_001: Yes, the underworld. I summoned it here. You'll all\nfind it quite impermeable.
MID_SC14_14_m09: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_m09_001: Impossible! You are of the living and yet act as if\nyou have received Father's favor.
MID_SC14_14_m09_002: As if protected by the underworld itself!\nWho are you?
MID_SC14_14_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_e01_001: {SetColor=Gold}Acid everywhere!{SetColor=Default} Gods, like being inside a monster's\nstomach...
MID_SC14_14_e01_003: Acid melts stuff, right? I guess that means we\n{SetColor=Gold}shouldn't stand in it{SetColor=Default}!
MID_SC14_14_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_e02_001: The {SetColor=Gold}acid{SetColor=Default} on the floor keeps {SetColor=Gold}spreading and ebbing{SetColor=Default}...\nalmost like a living creature. How repulsive!
MID_SC14_14_e16: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_e16_001: So stubborn... Fine, then—I'll kill you myself!
MID_SC14_14_e17: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_e17_001: Open your eyes, Lord Guillermo! Please.
MID_SC14_14_e17_002: Do you not recognize your own daughter?
MID_SC14_14_e17_003: ...
MID_SC14_14_e18: <TH>
MID_SC14_14_e18_001: You won't get away with this.
MID_SC14_14_e18_002: I'm not letting you escape. I'm going to end this,\nhere and now!
MID_SC14_14_e18_003: Poor thing. You really believe you can defeat me?\nI hate to disappoint, but...
MID_SC14_15_m01: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m01_001: Thank you, all of you, for helping me come this far.\nI ask for your aid in this last fight.
MID_SC14_15_m01_002: Clear the way, so I can finally reach Bertrand!
MID_SC14_15_m01_003: I won't attempt to stop you any longer, milady.
MID_SC14_15_m01_004: I want you to survive. If this is what it takes for\nthat to happen, then I'll do what you need.
MID_SC14_15_m01_005: Yeah... I'm still not really sure revenge is OK.
MID_SC14_15_m01_006: But if it helps you get past this once and for all,\nthen...I've got your back, Leda!
MID_SC14_15_m01_007: It is my lady Kalla's desire that you achieve\nyour goal.
MID_SC14_15_m01_008: But I desire it for my own part as well. I want to see\nwhat lies at the end of your path.
MID_SC14_15_m01_009: Leave it aaall to us, Leilidahna.
MID_SC14_15_m01_010: Let nothing impede you from settling matters with\nthe White-Maned Demon!
MID_SC14_15_m02: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m02_001: You intend to go after Bertrand? I'm afraid I can't\nlet you do that.
MID_SC14_15_m02_002: You'll have to face me instead. Gaitz Legazpi!
MID_SC14_15_m03: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m03_001: Anything to help out my big brother!
MID_SC14_15_m04: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m04_001: Ohoho! Whaddaya say we grow a nice garden here—\nfill the arena with blossoms of blood?! Heh heh HEH!
MID_SC14_15_m04_002: How very tasteless. There are many flowers that\nwould be more suitable.
MID_SC14_15_m04_003: For example—myself. Yes, watch as Olympia blooms,\nto the dazzlement of the crowd!
MID_SC14_15_m05: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m05_001: This woman leapt into the arena, carving her way to\nthe finale, all to face the White-Maned Demon!
MID_SC14_15_m05_002: Ohhh... The next chapter of my masterwork is\ncooking at a quick boil!
MID_SC14_15_m06: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m06_001: Viceroy Guillermo's daughter.
MID_SC14_15_m06_002: At long last... At long last, you and I stand before\neach other.
MID_SC14_15_m06_003: What is this I'm feeling... Hatred? Joy? Something\nelse... More emotions than I can take in at once!
MID_SC14_15_m07: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m07_001: Your face is familiar. Did you and I meet that day\nas well?
MID_SC14_15_m07_002: While alive, Lord Guillermo spoke of you often as\nthe great general of Arago.
MID_SC14_15_m07_003: I...have my own thoughts on that, but for now, I set\nthem aside to serve milady!
MID_SC14_15_m08: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m08_001: I can't die... There is more I must do!
MID_SC14_15_m09: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_m09_001: Come now, Bertrand the White-Maned Demon.\nIt's just the two of us.
MID_SC14_15_m09_002: We were fated to fight today. One way or another,\nthis ends now. And I won't let anyone interfere!
MID_SC14_15_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e01_001: All I have to do is run straight up this path.\nThen Bertrand is mine!
MID_SC14_15_e02: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e02_001: I would advise, as our {SetColor=Gold}first priority{SetColor=Default}, we {SetColor=Gold}neutralize the\nartillery on either side{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SC14_15_e03: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e03_001: What?! The flames are spreading. Is someone\nresponsible for this?
MID_SC14_15_e04: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e04_001: Now he's trying to burn me to death. Whatever.\nHe'll die first!
MID_SC14_15_e05: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e05_001: Leda is coming for me. Everyone, intercept her!
MID_SC14_15_e06: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e06_001: Ready? Then it begins.
MID_SC14_15_e07: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e07_001: <DLG>Bertrand used Ruler's Awakening. His accuracy and attack power\nwill be increased until his next phase.
MID_SC14_15_e08: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e08_001: <DLG>Bertrand used Flash Awakening. His physical protection\nwill be increased until his next phase.
MID_SC14_15_e09: <TH>
MID_SC14_15_e09_001: <DLG>Bertrand used Storm Awakening. He has greater ability to dodge\nattacks and criticals until his next phase.
MID_SC14_XX_Rewind_e01: <TH>
MID_SC14_XX_Rewind_e01_001: Huh? The pouch of sand I got all those years ago.\nIt's glowing!